argin-top:9pt;text-align:center"><span><br/></span></div><div style="margin-top:9pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">48</span></div></div></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:63pt;width:100%"><div style="margin-top:9pt"><span><br/></span></div><div><span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline"><a style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline" href="#i99d00350ed2941428822c008ad41baa8_7">Table of Contents</a></span></div><div style="margin-top:6pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">ZIONS BANCORPORATION, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION AND SUBSIDIARIES</span></div></div><ix:continuation id="f-507-3" continuedAt="f-507-4"><div style="margin-top:9pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Fair Value Option for Certain Loans Held for Sale</span></div><div style="margin-top:3pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">We apply the fair value option to certain commercial real estate (&#8220;CRE&#8221;) loans designated for sale to third-party conduits for securitization and hedged with derivative instruments. This election reduces accounting volatility that would otherwise result from the mismatch between measuring loans held for sale at the lower of cost or fair value and derivatives at fair value, without requiring the application of hedge accounting. These loans are included in &#8220;Loans held for sale&#8221; on the consolidated balance sheet. Related fair value gains and losses are included in &#8220;Capital markets fees and income&#8221; on the consolidated statement of income, and accrued interest is included in &#8220;Interest and fees on loans.&#8221;</span></div><div style="margin-top:9pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">At June&#160;30, 2026 and December&#160;31, 2025, we had </span><span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-62" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:LoansHeldForSaleFairValueDisclosure" scale="6" id="f-637">51</ix:nonFraction> million</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-90" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:LoansHeldForSaleFairValueDisclosure" scale="6" id="f-638">71</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively, of loans measured at fair value, with a corresponding unpaid principal balance of </span><span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-64" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:LoansReceivableHeldForSaleAmount" scale="6" id="f-639">51</ix:nonFraction> million</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-92" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:LoansReceivableHeldForSaleAmount" scale="6" id="f-640">72</ix:nonFraction> million. During the first six months of 2026 and 2025, we recognized approximately</span><span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-117" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:FairValueOptionCreditRiskGainsLossesOnAssets" scale="6" id="f-641">7</ix:nonFraction> million</span><sp